The context manager allows users to direct traces to specific projects/log streams

Also:
- Flushing traces when the python interpreter exits
- Adding more examples to the test script

```
@log(span_type="llm")
def call_openai():
    chat_completion = client.chat.completions.create(
        messages=[
            {
                "role": "user",
                "content": "Say this is a test",
            }
        ],
        model="gpt-4o",
    )

    return chat_completion.choices[0].message.content


@log()
def make_nested_call():
    return call_openai()


# This will log to the default project and log stream specified in your environment variables
content = make_nested_call()
print(content)

# This will log to the project and log stream specified in the context manager
with galileo_context(project="gen-ai-project", log_stream="test2"):
    content = make_nested_call()
    print(content)
```

